    "body": "## Motivation\n\nTriton specializes int args by value (`== 1`, `% 16 == 0`, other) and the mHC split-K kernels take the row count as a plain int. So any batch whose row count lands in a new class recompiles mid-serving on the scheduler thread while the other ranks wait on it.\n\n```\nTriton kernel '_hc_mix_reduce_sinkhorn_kernel' took 28.57 s to compile after serving started.\n```\n\nOn DSV4.1-Flash (4xB200, 8k prompts, 16 concurrency) this showed up as an 11.6 s P99 TTFT vs a 76 ms median.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdd the row count to `do_not_specialize` in `_hc_mix_reduce_sinkhorn_kernel` (`m`), `_hc_mix_stats_partial_kernel` (`M`) and `_hc_mix_stats_bf16x3_kernel` (`M`). Specialization is not useful since it's only used in the bounds check and per-row offsets.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOutputs of all three wrappers are bitwise identical to main for m in {1, 16, 17, 33, 48, 128, 145, 4000, 4096, 8192, 8193}.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n1xB200, V4.1 shapes, empty Triton cache, calls in sequence:\n\n| Call | main | this PR |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| generic, m=17 after m=16 | 11.0 s | 0.2 ms |\n| generic, m=1 | 10.5 s | 131 ms |\n| deepgemm, m=145 after m=128 | 1.8 s | 0.1 ms |\n| bf16x3, m=8193 after m=8192 | 1.2 s | 0.2 ms |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39215524823](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39215524823)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39215524806](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39215524806)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39215524951](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39215524951)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
